From aa4fe5eee3c4c3f7ab7ff34c02da0119cc605137 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rohit Agrawal <rohit.agrawal@databricks.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Jan 2026 06:25:40 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] cluster: add a new composite cluster with retries across
 multiple sub-clusters (#42618)

## Description

The existing aggregate cluster implements fallback between sub-clusters
based on the health of sub-cluster endpoints. In this PR we are adding a
new cluster type called composite cluster that allows retries to use
cluster that is different from the original request.

**Example:**

```yaml
- name: composite_cluster
  connect_timeout: 2s
  lb_policy: CLUSTER_PROVIDED
  cluster_type:
    name: envoy.clusters.composite
    typed_config:
      "@type": type.googleapis.com/envoy.extensions.clusters.composite.v3.ClusterConfig
      clusters:
      - primary_cluster
      - secondary_cluster
      - fallback_cluster
      overflow_option: USE_LAST_CLUSTER
```

Fix https://github.com/envoyproxy/envoy/issues/40264

---

**Commit Message:** cluster: add a new composite cluster with retries
across multiple sub-clusters
**Additional Description:** Adding a new Composite Cluster which allows
retries across multiple sub-clusters.
**Risk Level:** Low
**Testing**: Added Unit & Integration Tests
**Docs Changes:** Added
**Release Notes:** Added

